              "fill": "$ink-soft",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "two-step jagati plinth whose lower step follows the slope (flat top at the highest ground point, retaining wall with stone courses below) · vedibandha mouldings · jangha wall with bhadra and pratiratha projections · door with lintel · shikhara of receding bhumi tiers (curvilinear taper, width = w·(1 − 0.5·f^1.6)) · corner bhumi-amalakas every third tier · griva · ribbed amalaka · kalasha. Right: a cluster of 9 on a shared levelled terrace. Scattered valley shrines use the same function at 22–64 px.",
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
